From: Nipuna H Herath <nipunaherath@hotmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 15:15:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 10/16] CUDA/HIP: one kernel for one token of attention over
 stored states (depth mix)

Inkling 2 mixes its block outputs with learned queries before each attention,
FFN and output (block attention residuals): RMS_NORM(cur) -> TRANSPOSE ->
CONCAT(blocks_t, cur_t) -> CONCAT(blocks, cur) -> MUL_MAT(states, query) ->
SOFT_MAX -> MUL_MAT(states_t, scores), 120 times per token. For one token, up
to 8 states and 4 queries this runs as one 1024-thread block: one pass sums the
squares of cur and all dot products (those of rms_norm(cur) are those of cur
times the norm factor), one reduction, a softmax per query, and a pass that
writes the weighted sums. The concatenated states are never written.

R9700 Inkling-2-Mini UD-Q8_K_XL tg128 44.1 -> 46.3 tok/s, 3653 -> 3078
kernels per token; KLD vs the original build 0.0020 at batch 1. New
test-backend-ops case DEPTH_MIX.
